# tsup (via bundle-require) writes a transient
# `<config>.bundled_<random>.{mjs,cjs}` next to config files while it runs,
# then deletes it. Formatting isn't ordered against builds, so a check can
# catch the file mid-existence and fail with ENOENT. Same reason the ESLint
# config ignores this pattern.
*.bundled_*.mjs
*.bundled_*.cjs
